Whisper: Whisper Canary has a profile folder of its own

What: builds on the update channel "canary" imply MOZ_APP_PROFILE "Whisper Canary",
so Whisper Canary keeps its profiles in %APPDATA%\Whisper Canary (Windows) and
~/.config/whisper canary (Linux) instead of Whisper's Whisper\Whisper and
~/.config/whisper/whisper.
Why: the canary is installed next to Whisper and must not open, change or share its
profiles. MOZ_APP_PROFILE can only be implied by configure (not set in a mozconfig),
like MOZ_APP_VENDOR in patches/0001-app-identity.patch.
---
diff --git a/browser/moz.configure b/browser/moz.configure
--- a/browser/moz.configure
+++ b/browser/moz.configure
@@ -20,6 +20,17 @@
 imply_option("BROWSER_CHROME_URL", "chrome://browser/content/browser.xhtml")
 
 
+# Whisper: Whisper Canary (update channel "canary") keeps its profile apart from
+# Whisper's: %APPDATA%\Whisper Canary on Windows, ~/.config/whisper canary on Linux.
+@depends(update_channel)
+def whisper_app_profile(channel):
+    if channel == "canary":
+        return "Whisper Canary"
+
+
+imply_option("MOZ_APP_PROFILE", whisper_app_profile, reason="--enable-update-channel")
+
+
 with only_when(target_has_linux_kernel & compile_environment):
     option(env="MOZ_NO_PIE_COMPAT", help="Enable non-PIE wrapper")
 
